<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis XII of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1462">1462</a>–<a href="/years/1515">1515</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Father of the People</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis XII, born at Blois as duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1498. He had his first marriage annulled to marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany">Anne of Brittany</a>, widow of Charles VIII, keeping Brittany tied to the crown. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a> he conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in 1499 and briefly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinois">Valentinois</a> a duchy for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a>. Popular for low taxes, he was called the Father of the People.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france.jpg" alt="Louis XII of France" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Jean Perréal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwig_XII._von_Frankreich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
